    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463-a5">

                <pb facs="0634" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg538"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 82.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitchcock to Mr.
                            Smith.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May 30,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of May 28, inclosing letter
                    from Dr. Michaels and physician’s certificate, duly received. I have to say in
                    this matter that Dr. Michaels fails entirely to point out what the illness was
                    from <pb facs="0635" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/> which his son was suffering when
                    he so urgently required a passport in order to go to him, and Mr. S. Michaels’s
                    illness does not appear to have been of a nature which would prevent his going
                    to his son in case of the urgent need represented.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ethan A. Hitchcock.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
